// =============================================================================
// STSH — CANONICAL smoke_alarm_monitor INIT ARTIFACT (lane A-7)
// =============================================================================
// Interface: canisters/smoke-alarm-monitor/smoke_alarm_monitor.did:99 —
// `service : (MonitorInit) -> {…}` (MonitorInit at :9-20).
//
// THE CONFIG IS IMMUTABLE AND THE CANISTER IS BLACKHOLED AT LAUNCH. There are
// no setters. Every value below is permanent; `validate_config`
// (canisters/smoke-alarm-monitor/src/lib.rs:840) traps at install on an
// anonymous/management principal, an interval below the minimum, a staleness
// bound tighter than the interval, or a capacity outside 1..=4096 — which makes
// install the LAST point at which a wrong value is still fixable.
//
// Principals (RECORD_J18_VAULT_BIRTHS_2026-09-12.md):
//   token_canister          stsh_token     clv7x-haaaa-aaaar-qchha-cai  (prop 5)
//   pool_principal          shielded_pool  cxrfg-qaaaa-aaaar-qchfa-cai  (prop 1)
//   treasury_principal      treasury       cqqds-5yaaa-aaaar-qchfq-cai  (prop 2)
//   pool_attestation_source shielded_pool  cxrfg-qaaaa-aaaar-qchfa-cai  (prop 1)
// `treasury_principal` is the account weighed for stray funds THROUGH THE
// TOKEN's icrc1_balance_of — the monitor never calls the treasury (did:12-14).
// `pool_attestation_source` is the canister exposing get_solvency_attestation,
// which is the pool itself (did:15-16) — the two pool fields are deliberately
// separate knobs that happen to take the same value today.
//
// Cadence (canisters/smoke-alarm-monitor/OPERATIONS.md:16-18):
//   refresh_interval_ns 300_000_000_000   =  5 min
//   max_staleness_ns    900_000_000_000   = 15 min  (>= interval, enforced)
//   history_capacity    288               = 24 h at the 5-min cadence
//
// INSTALL ORDER — THIS CANISTER GOES LAST. `init` arms a zero-delay timer that
// performs an immediate first refresh (src/lib.rs:633-641), which reads the
// token, the pool and the treasury balance. Installed before them, the monitor
// comes up on a CallFailed snapshot and retries on the next interval — not a
// brick, but a monitor whose first published snapshot is red for no real
// reason. Install it after every source it reads.
//
// This monitor reads the POOL ATTESTATION. It is NOT the reserves.stsh.fi page
// (that is the `solvency_status` asset canister, pyeop-7yaaa-aaaam-ajfja-cai).
//
// The operator page uploads smoke_alarm_monitor_init.bin verbatim;
// `expected_arg_hash` is the sha256 of that .bin (a7_install_kit.toml).
// =============================================================================
(
  record {
    token_canister          = principal "clv7x-haaaa-aaaar-qchha-cai";
    pool_principal          = principal "cxrfg-qaaaa-aaaar-qchfa-cai";
    treasury_principal      = principal "cqqds-5yaaa-aaaar-qchfq-cai";
    pool_attestation_source = principal "cxrfg-qaaaa-aaaar-qchfa-cai";
    refresh_interval_ns     = 300_000_000_000 : nat64;
    max_staleness_ns        = 900_000_000_000 : nat64;
    history_capacity        = 288 : nat32;
  },
)
